 34AL    34MG B- DECAY (44.9 MS)       2017LI03                  ENSDF    202609
 34AL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34AL dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 20-May-2026)          
 34AL c  2017Li03: {+34}Mg ions were produced by fragmentation between a 1.4-GeV
 34AL2c  pulsed proton beam from the Proton Synchrotron Booster and a UC{-x}    
 34AL3c  target at ISOLDE-CERN. The Mg atoms that diffused out of the target    
 34AL4c  matrix were selectively laser ionized using the resonance ionization   
 34AL5c  laser ion source (RILIS) and accelerated to 40 keV. A=34 nuclei were   
 34AL6c  selected by the ISOLDE General Purpose Separator and implanted onto a  
 34AL7c  movable tape located at the center of the ISOLDE Decay station. The    
 34AL8c  {+34}Mg beam rate is 700 pps {I1}. |b particles were detected using a  
 34AL9c  3-cm-thick NE102 plastic scintillator. |g rays were detected using five
 34ALAc  HPGe clover detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |b|g-coin, and |b|g|g-coin.  
 34ALBc  Deduced levels, J, |p, decay branching ratios, log {Ift}, T{-1/2} and  
 34ALCc  %|b{+-}n of parent. Comparisons with large-scale shell-model           
 34ALDc  calculations using the SDPF-U-MIX interaction.                         
 34AL c  1984La03: Sodium isotopes were produced via the fragmentation of a 30  
 34AL2c  g/cm{+2} iridium target by 10-GeV protons from the CERN synchrotron.   
 34AL3c  The recoiling nuclear fragments are thermalized in heated graphite. The
 34AL4c  alkali elements selectively diffuse out of the target, are surface     
 34AL5c  ionized, and analyzed by the online mass spectrometer, then focused at 
 34AL6c  the bottom of a well-shaped NE213 liquid scintillator neutron detector.
 34AL7c  |b particles were detected using a well-shaped thin plastic            
 34AL8c  scintillator. Measured |b and neutron counts. Deduced the T{-1/2} of   
 34AL9c  {+34}Mg. P{-n} values were reported for other Mg isotopes but not for  
 34ALAc  {+34}Mg.                                                               
 34AL c  1999YoZW (RIKEN Report): {+9}Be({+48}Ca,X) and {+181}Ta({+48}Ca,X).    
 34AL2c  Measured T{-1/2} and %|b{+-}n.                                         
 34AL cB IB$From I(|g+ce) intensity balances at each level.                     
 34AL cG E,RI$From 2017Li03 and 2017LiZZ: e-mail reply from A. Negret and R.    
 34AL2cG Lica. E|g systematic uncertainty of 0.1 keV from calibration added in  
 34AL3cG quadrature to the statistical uncertainties provided in 2017LiZZ.      
 34AL cL E$From a least-squares fit to |g-ray energies.                         
 34AL cL J,T$From the Adopted Levels.                                           
